      <p>
        Since the system requires high system head and low flow rate, centrifugal pumps are not suitable. However, among the many positive displacement (PD) pumps, with the pressure water pump being the most optimal, the flow rate and maximum head provided still did not meet the requirements, considering that the pump head versus flow rate of PD pumps are nearly vertical, we assume a linear line graph of gradient XX to compare.
        Cost between both systems? Cost of pump and cost of pipe (and fittings?).
      </p>
      <image-component tag="image" source="assets/tt_final/pump_curve.jpg"
        subtitle="Table XXX: Head vs flow rate for 3/4 pipe with PD pump"></image-component>
